**Read:** Complete the assigned cleaning chapter, NVR main report, interfacial/colloid chapters and selected full semiconductor articles before defending the three investigations.

Join chemical identity, physical transfer, observation and useful function. A residue investigation asks what the method recovers; a rinse investigation asks where material travels; a sensitive-manufacturing investigation asks whether removal preserves the object. The same Records and calculations can support all three.

**Work:** Complete each investigation, beginning with the hypothetical balances and advancing to a published method or result. Retain assumptions, uncertainty, alternative explanations and unobserved quantities. If experimental resources are unavailable, make the analytical reconstruction reproducible and identify precisely what remains empirically untested.

**Return:** [Clean manufacturing and contamination control — from familiar objects to controlled processes](../Clean-manufacturing-and-contamination-control.lingua#r_7D8SQ8BVQDZQBDBGC6DP0JAMZN).
**Continue in clean manufacturing:** [Defend a residue collection and identification result](Defend-a-residue-collection-and-identification-result.lingua#r_3416ZR1G2ZCSREBGQ101TWP2V5), [Defend a rinse, dry and preservation system](Defend-a-rinse-dry-and-preservation-system.lingua#r_07NVYTM0NA06NSBRY7WK29MXC7), [Defend cleaning without losing the manufactured function](Defend-cleaning-without-losing-the-manufactured-function.lingua#r_188DKZBJJETJFPKYH27SH91AQE).

